feat: Add individual table name replacement support to validation

Enhanced validation step to support replacing not only catalog and schema
names, but also individual table names. This addresses scenarios where table
names differ between environments (e.g., dev.sales.customer_data vs
prod.analytics.customers).

Key Changes:
- Added update_config_catalog_schema_table() function for individual table replacement
- Enhanced prompt_catalog_schema_replacement() with two-mode support:
  1. Bulk mode: Replace catalog.schema for all tables at once
  2. Individual mode: Replace catalog.schema.table one by one
- Comprehensive updates across all configuration sections:
  * Table definitions (catalog, schema, table names)
  * SQL expressions and queries
  * Join specifications and conditions
  * Join aliases (e.g., orders → transactions updates orders.id → transactions.id)
  * Benchmark questions (expected_sql and table fields)
  * Instructions (table references in content)
- Enhanced update_config_catalog_schema() to include joins
- Interactive prompts with press-Enter-to-keep-current-value UX
- Up to 3 validation attempts with automatic re-validation

Testing:
- Added comprehensive test suite in tests/test_table_name_replacement.py
- 4 new tests covering individual updates, bulk updates, preservation, and alias updates
- All 24 validation-related tests pass (4 new + 20 existing)

Documentation:
- Updated README.md with interactive replacement examples
- Updated ARCHITECTURE.md with detailed feature description
- Added change_logs/table_name_replacement.md with complete documentation

Benefits:
- Handles both simple (catalog/schema) and complex (table name) differences
- Interactive prompts prevent accidental bulk changes
- Automatic updates to all references (SQL, joins, benchmarks, etc.)
- Backward compatible - existing workflows continue to work
- Safe - updates join aliases to match new table names

